>A way to make searching less boring is to use an item which has 
>intrinsic searching.  For lawful characters, the easiest item to
>obtain is Excalibur (via dipping a long sword for a level 5+ character).
>Just wield it and walk around, traps and hidden doors reveal themselves
>as you walk by.  What fun!  I don't know which other items have this
>capability, can anyone add to the list?

Play an archeologist, an elf, a rogue, a barabarian, or a tourist.
All get searching as an intrinsic at some level.  Elves start 
with it (as well as several others).  

The non-artifact that gets you searching is (obviously) a ring of
searching.  If you have an extra one, see what it's made of, then
if possible polymorph into an appropriate creature and eat it.
(Rock moles, xorns, and gelatinous cubes are possible ring-eaters.)
This doesn't always work, but it's worth a try if you have an extra
ring or an easy way (WoP) of making more.  

When searching for the magic portals at the end, wearing the Amulet,
as noted before, is better.  It gives you little clues like "you 
feel warm" or "very warm" or "hot."  Better range than searching.
Important, when you're up to your ears in Archons.

